WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:03.920
It's official: The folks at Dunder Mifflin
are moving out.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.460
As hard as it is to hear, the beloved sitcom
The Office is leaving Netflix.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:12.510
The streaming giant confirmed the news on
Tuesday, June 25th, tweeting that The Office

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:16.160
will remain in its content library until January
2021.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.300
Then, it's gone from Netflix for good.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.800
"Why am I so sad?

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.380
Am I doing the wrong thing?

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.610
Absolutely not.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.560
It's just that sometimes, goodbyes are a bitch."

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.070
Before you start sobbing into your "World's
Best Boss" mugs, you should know that it's

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:32.900
not all bad.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.500
Viewers who fell in love with The Office can
still binge the series from the comfort of

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.610
their own homes.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.880
They'll just have to do it on a different
streaming platform.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.840
Starting in 2021, The Office will be available
to watch on NBCUniversal's yet-to-release

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:45.910
streaming service.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:49.960
The Office's quirky cast of characters and
its witty storylines have found a place in

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.969
millions of viewers' hearts over the years.

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:56.720
In 2018, Netflix subscribers spent more time
watching The Office than any other television

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.780
series available to stream on the platform,
so as hard as the show's departure will be

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.690
for viewers, it may be even harder for Netflix.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:04.680
"That's what she said!”

00:01:07.069 --> 00:01:11.899
The reason why The Office is leaving Netflix
is because NBCUniversal, which owns the series,

00:01:11.899 --> 00:01:16.869
has decided to remove it from the steaming
platform and bring it to its own service.

00:01:16.869 --> 00:01:20.439
NBCUniversal previously licensed The Office
to Netflix, but now that the series' current

00:01:20.439 --> 00:01:25.390
deal with the service is about to expire and
NBCUniversal's yet-unnamed platform is expected

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:30.139
to launch in the middle of 2020, it isn't
advantageous for NBCUniversal to continue

00:01:30.139 --> 00:01:32.259
granting streaming rights to Netflix.

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:36.959
According to The Hollywood Reporter, the company
has secured exclusive domestic streaming rights

00:01:36.959 --> 00:01:42.369
for all nine seasons of The Office in a five-year
deal, paying a staggering $100 million per

00:01:42.369 --> 00:01:44.860
year to stream it on its upcoming platform.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.979
"Man, that is a lot of guacamole.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.399
Lot of the green.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:49.640
Lot of green."

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.740
NBCUniversal executives are incredibly excited
that The Office is shifting from Netflix to

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:58.820
the impending streaming service, with the
company's chairman of direct-to-consumer and

00:01:58.829 --> 00:02:01.069
digital enterprises Bonnie Hammer saying,

00:02:01.069 --> 00:02:05.639
"The Office has become a staple of pop-culture
and is a rare gem whose relevance continues

00:02:05.639 --> 00:02:09.369
to grow at a time when fans have more entertainment
choices than ever before.

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:14.220
We can't wait to welcome the gang from Dunder
Mifflin to NBCUniversal's new streaming service."

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:18.700
When Netflix addressed the situation, it took
a slight jab at NBCUniversal in mentioning

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:23.560
that Office fans can continue watching the
series ad-free until January 2021.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:27.420
By contrast, NBCUniversal's streaming service
is "ad-supported."

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:33.430
The move to have The Office leave Netflix
has been in progress for some time now.

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:39.500
In April 2019, it was reported that NBCUniversal
brass were engaging in, quote, "internal discussions

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:44.850
about removing The Office from Netflix when
the contract expires in 2021" and subsequently

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.000
loading it onto the new streaming site.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:51.390
This is exactly what happened with Friends,
another much-adored sitcom that originally

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:52.660
aired on NBC.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:53.220
Warner Bros.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:58.040
Television produced and distributed Friends,
and Netflix paid a pretty penny to keep the

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:59.770
series in its library year after year.

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:03.830
Though it was briefly believed at the end
of 2018 that Friends would leave the platform

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:09.380
in January 2019, the truth is that it's sticking
around until sometime in 2020, when WarnerMedia's

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.960
new streaming site enters the arena.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:15.700
WarnerMedia intends to use Friends as a major
selling point for the new platform, and it's

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:19.220
likely that NBCUniversal wants to do the same
with The Office.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:23.330
With The Office and so many other wonderful
shows getting plucked from Netflix, the platform

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:27.020
is going to have to ramp up its original content
to keep subscribers around.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:32.860
Netflix has great original series like Stranger
Things, BoJack Horseman, GLOW, The Crown,

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.290
and more in its catalogue - but it remains
to be seen whether those shows will ever be

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.890
able to fill the void The Office will leave
behind.

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:43.340
All we can do for now is enjoy it while it's
here, and remember what a wise man once said:

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:45.200
"WHERE ARE THE TURTLES?"

